This print depicts a screech of 6 black headed seagulls and 3 ice cream cones. It is hand-printed using a baren, and blocks and stamps carved out of Japanese vinyl. The blocks are used for the birds, the stamps for the ice creams.

![design details](/images/ice-cream-thieves-1.jpg)

The design is based on an einstein tessellation. Here, "einstein" derives from two German words "ein" and "stein", meaning "one stone": a single shape can tile a flat surface without any gaps. Astonishingly, the tessellation is _aperiodic_. That is, however large the surface, the pattern will never repeat.

I live by the sea, and admire the seagulls' acrobatic flight. If there's any sign of food they fight for it.

